<title>BELGIUM: PetroFina joins Alaskan oilfield venture.</title>
<headline>PetroFina joins Alaskan oilfield venture.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian oil and chemicals group PetroFina said on Friday it would take part in the development of the Badami oilfield to the east of Prudhoe Bay in Alaska at a cost of $300 million.</p>
<p>The field, due to come on stream in late 1998, is assessed as having recoverable reserves of 120 million barrels of oil. Production is expected to peak in 1999 at 35,000 barrels per day. It will be sent down the Trans-Alaska pipeline to Valdez on the southern coast of Alaska.</p>
<p>The field, in which BP has a 70 percent stake against PetroFina's 30 percent, was discovered in 1990.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
